{"parentUuid":"08ad07b6-f3fd-4a1a-a06b-ccec30c3f6c4","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ac8d66f27603101d9","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfY5hR6QmJE1tTUiQqCZP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011BrajAiJS5DU8NrQWAqPVQ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/user/skills/engine-skill-framework && grep -n \"^#\" docs/00-design-principles.md; grep -n -i \"dispute\\|arbitrat\\|subtree\\|workstream\" docs/00-design-principles.md | head -30","description":"Find dispute rules in principles"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2876,"cache_read_input_tokens":75656,"output_tokens":406,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":247},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2876},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":406,"cache_read_input_tokens":75656,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2876,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2876,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_011BrajAiJS5DU8NrQWAqPVQ":{"command":"cd /home/user/skills/engine-skill-framework && grep -n \"^#\" docs/00-design-principles.md; grep -n -i \"dispute\\|arbitrat\\|subtree\\|workstream\" docs/00-design-principles.md | head -30","description":"Find dispute rules in principles"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfY5hQeNRdnfYRHbvbV5Y","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"6fb5e523-9dee-4f3f-b395-805be7c443ce","timestamp":"2026-09-29T16:55:29.973Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan"}
{"parentUuid":"6fb5e523-9dee-4f3f-b395-805be7c443ce","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"10d83fbe-32cf-4872-a1ef-e8cfbcf10d96","agentId":"ac8d66f27603101d9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011BrajAiJS5DU8NrQWAqPVQ","type":"tool_result","content":"1:# 00 · Design Principles of the Skill Framework\n5:## 1. What a skill is\n18:## 2. Tiers and kinds\n37:## 3. Skills depend on contracts, never on skills\n49:## 4. Ownership patterns used to resolve overlaps\n66:## 5. Scaling down is proven, not asserted\n84:## 6. Default architectural stances\n104:## 7. Technique maturity and the radar\n110:## 8. Specific boundary decisions\n131:## 9. What phase 1 deliberately does not decide\n22:| Orchestrator | 4 | `engine-architect` (boundaries, profiles, arbitration across workstreams), `architecture-governance` (ADRs, fitness functions, radar, anti-legacy catalogue, critic calibration, adjudication and the independence matrix), `program-orchestration` (agent coordination, milestones, ledger, triage), `engine-product-management` (roadmap and game-team intake: the engine as a product). |\n35:**Workstreams** (foundation, platform, content, world, rendering, simulation, audio, online, gameplay, UI, tools, release, quality, performance, governance, assurance) group skills for delegated arbitration and staffing. They are also the co-hosting unit, so the independence matrix (`data/crosscutting.json`: decider vs reviewer, builder vs adjudicator, implementer vs oracle author) is enforced by keeping each pair in different workstreams. A dispute inside one lead's subtree is settled by that lead. Only cross-workstream disputes reach `engine-architect` (`ARCH.ORG.escalation`).\n51:Five patterns resolve almost every boundary dispute. Each is applied by name, so a critic can check that it was applied consistently.\n59:- **Domain editor = domain tool logic + editor host.** Every user-facing runtime domain owns its authoring logic in a `<DOMAIN>.TOOL` capability, for example `RND.TOOL.material-editor`, `ANM.TOOL.retarget-editor` or `GAM.TOOL.ai-editors`. The editor skills provide the host through `C-EDCMD` (serializable commands, undo, selection), `C-EDHOST` (asset-editor host, thumbnails, curves and timelines), `C-EDVIEW` (viewport tool modes, brushes, picking, gizmos, preview worlds), `C-GRAPH` and `C-VCS`. `check.py` fails any skill that owns tool logic but reaches the editor through no contract, any world tool that does not reach `C-EDVIEW`, and any user-facing runtime domain whose subtree owns no authoring capability and records no reason.\n82:Organizational scale-down is handled separately. A small effort co-hosts the skills of one workstream in one agent (`ARCH.ORG.staffing`), and the governance weight per organization tier is defined in `ARCH.GOV.process-tiers`.\n99:| All IO is asynchronous and staged (IO → decompress → fixup → upload → publish), with deadlines and cross-pool arbitration under one physical budget; GPU-side transfers and decompression are arbitrated by the render graph (`RND.GRAPH.external-work`). | Synchronous loads; page-fault streaming; independent streaming pools that compete. | NVMe throughput requires deep queues. On UMA hardware, texture, geometry, audio and BVH pools share one memory. |\n118:| Views are arbitrated in `spatial-transforms` (`C-VIEW`). Gameplay cameras, cinematics, editor, photo mode and XR are sources of views. | The editor and XR must drive views without the gameplay layer, and listeners, streaming sources and LWC origins derive from the active view. |","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"e0c1a85e-a53a-40ad-b0ea-2f5df674a1f1","timestamp":"2026-09-29T16:55:30.035Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6fb5e523-9dee-4f3f-b395-805be7c443ce","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan"}
