ss-subsystem data channels\",\n \"summary\": \"Versioned snapshots, double/triple-buffered hand-off, mailboxes and multi-rate resampling between subsystems; producer/consumer declared per channel. The default for runtime data flow; global barriers need an ADR.\",\n \"requires\": [\n  \"C-FRAME\"\n ],\n \"conformance\": true,\n \"oracle_author\": \"input-system\"\n}\n['C-UI', 'C-BUILD', 'C-DEVUI']","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"35acfc7b-e7fb-4ef3-96f7-93ef7432d9b8","timestamp":"2026-09-29T16:55:57.197Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"16dfb241-00a5-4a57-aa6b-f095207f2af3","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan"}
