es\", \"E\", [\"test-architect\"]]\n22:| Orchestrator | 4 | `engine-architect` (boundaries, profiles, arbitration across workstreams), `architecture-governance` (ADRs, fitness functions, radar, anti-legacy catalogue, critic calibration, adjudication and the independence matrix), `program-orchestration` (agent coordination, milestones, ledger, triage), `engine-product-management` (roadmap and game-team intake: the engine as a product). |\n76:`check.py` proves all 34 named configurations are closed. These run from `indie-2d-online-moddable-server` (61 build skills), `online-3d-bot-client` (68), `mobile-async-client` (70) and `minimal-client` (75) up to `aaa-open-world-online-tools` (123). Every configuration is claimed by exactly one milestone, which proves it buildable by then. Capability-level profile tags provide finer gating inside a skill:\n102:| Instrumentation, tests, budgets and determinism levels exist before features (milestone gates from M0). Every code contract has an oracle author who is not its sole implementer; acceptance suites are read-only for implementers and have sealed holdouts. | Profiling and testing added late; implementers grading their own tests. | Performance claims need measurement, and autonomous implementers can game tests they control. |","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"23e47885-ee1e-472e-ade5-79fcdd206215","timestamp":"2026-09-29T16:58:38.788Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"305b48c0-7be6-4e32-8109-9efa02279d45","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan"}
